														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-1640621">
									

<p>I like this (and definitely am upvoting it). Lest anyone question, I <em>did</em> give blessing for this to implicitly or explicitly reference 1050.</p>
<p>Don't get me wrong, I like the possibility that the Foundation may have found more information that might have to do with 1050. That said, I have misgivings about the 1050 losing its ambiguity. In other words, in 1050 I try and clearly demarcate what the Foundation <em>knows</em> (fact) and what the Foundation <em>thinks</em> (speculation). If something comes out and attempts to definitively say &quot;hey, this definitely [dis]proves this bit of speculation about 1050&quot;, I'm going to oppose it. So, I encourage making the apparent link a little more speculative - the Foundation can't know definitively that 1980-5 is anything like 1050's Destroyers. I'm not sure how to go about doing that, but that's my thoughts.</p>
<p>Also, I do not mind (or think it would detract) if you redact &quot;1050&quot; to the blackbox state. Just saying.</p>

							</div>

								
					
